import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe16.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope and Definition" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Two Categories — Asset-Related and Income-Related Grants" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Grants Related to Assets — Deferred Income Treatment" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. THE KEY DIVERGENCE — No Asset-Deduction Presentation Alternative" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Grants Related to Income" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Recognition Criteria" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — a Grant Related to an Asset" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — a Grant Compensating for Costs Already Incurred" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IAS 20" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 政府补助 · Deferred income presentation only — the asset-deduction alternative under IAS 20 is not permitted · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Monetary or non-monetary assistance received free of charge</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 16 governs the RECOGNITION and MEASUREMENT of GOVERNMENT GRANTS — MONETARY or NON-MONETARY assets RECEIVED from the GOVERNMENT FREE of charge — EXCLUDING state INVESTMENT and OTHER capital contributions TREATED as owners' EQUITY. The Standard is BROADLY converged with IAS 20 internationally, WITH one NOTABLE presentation-related DIVERGENCE (Section 5).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope and Definition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Assistance received without an equivalent exchange</div><div class="principle">A GOVERNMENT GRANT is MONETARY or NON-MONETARY ASSISTANCE received from the GOVERNMENT FREE of charge — EXCLUDING government ACTIONS taken in its CAPACITY as an OWNER (e.g. CAPITAL contributions treated as an EQUITY investment, WHICH are OUTSIDE this Standard's SCOPE).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Two Categories — Asset-Related and Income-Related Grants</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Classified by the nature of the underlying condition</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Grants related to assets</span><span>REQUIRE the PURCHASE, CONSTRUCTION, or OTHERWISE formation of a LONG-TERM asset</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Grants related to income</span><span>ALL other GRANTS, NOT tied to the FORMATION of a LONG-term asset</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Grants Related to Assets — Deferred Income Treatment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Amortised systematically over the asset's useful life</div><div class="text-supporting">A GRANT related to an ASSET is RECOGNISED as DEFERRED INCOME (a LIABILITY), AMORTISED to PROFIT or LOSS on a SYSTEMATIC and RATIONAL basis OVER the useful LIFE of the RELATED asset — MATCHING the GRANT'S recognition to the PERIOD over WHICH the underlying ASSET generates ECONOMIC benefits.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — No Asset-Deduction Presentation Alternative</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Only one presentation method is permitted</div><div class="text-supporting">IAS 20 PERMITS an ENTITY to PRESENT an ASSET-related grant EITHER as DEFERRED income, OR ALTERNATIVELY by DEDUCTING the GRANT from the ASSET'S carrying AMOUNT (REDUCING the DEPRECIATION charge over the ASSET'S life INSTEAD of RECOGNISING separate GRANT income). ASBE No. 16 permits ONLY the DEFERRED INCOME presentation — the ASSET-deduction ALTERNATIVE is NOT available. WHILE BOTH methods PRODUCE the SAME net PROFIT impact over TIME, this is a GENUINELY notable PRESENTATION-level divergence, SIMPLIFYING and STANDARDISING Chinese PRACTICE relative to the CHOICE IAS 20 permits internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Grants Related to Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Matched to the period of related costs, or recognised immediately</div><div class="text-supporting">A GRANT related to INCOME intended to COMPENSATE for FUTURE related COSTS or LOSSES is RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS OVER the period the RELATED costs are RECOGNISED. A GRANT received as COMPENSATION for EXPENSES or LOSSES ALREADY incurred is RECOGNISED IMMEDIATELY in PROFIT or LOSS for the PERIOD it becomes RECEIVABLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Recognition Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Reasonable assurance of compliance and receipt</div><div class="text-supporting">A GOVERNMENT grant is RECOGNISED ONLY where THERE is REASONABLE ASSURANCE that the ENTERPRISE will COMPLY with any CONDITIONS attached to the GRANT, and that the GRANT will ACTUALLY be RECEIVED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a Grant Related to an Asset</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Deferred income, amortised over the asset's life</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A government subsidy for a new production line</div><div class="wk-body">A company receives an RMB 12,000,000 government grant to purchase new manufacturing equipment with an estimated 10-year useful life.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises the RMB 12,000,000 as DEFERRED INCOME, AMORTISING it to profit or LOSS over the 10-year useful LIFE: RMB 12,000,000 ÷ 10 = <strong>RMB 1,200,000 per year</strong> — RECOGNISED as a SEPARATE line of GRANT income, RATHER than REDUCING the equipment's OWN carrying amount (an OPTION unavailable under ASBE No. 16).</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Grant Compensating for Costs Already Incurred</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Immediate recognition in profit or loss</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A retrospective disaster-relief subsidy</div><div class="wk-body">A company receives an RMB 3,000,000 government subsidy compensating it for flood-related losses already incurred in the prior period.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises the FULL RMB 3,000,000 IMMEDIATELY in PROFIT or LOSS in the CURRENT period — since it COMPENSATES for COSTS/losses ALREADY incurred, RATHER than FUTURE costs to be MATCHED over TIME.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 16 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and amounts of government grants recognised, by category</span><span>Unfulfilled conditions and other contingencies attached to recognised grants</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether "reasonable assurance" of compliance and receipt exists</span><span>Classifying a grant as asset-related or income-related</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Amortisation period for asset-related grants, linked to the related asset's useful life</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 20</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 16 vs IAS 20</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 16</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 20</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Asset-related grant presentation</span><span>Deferred income ONLY</span><span>Deferred income OR asset-deduction, as a policy choice</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Income-related grant timing</span><span>Matched to related costs, or immediate</span><span>Matched to related costs, or immediate — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A NARROW but genuine PRESENTATION divergence — the UNDERLYING recognition and MEASUREMENT principles are OTHERWISE thoroughly CONVERGED with IAS 20.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every government grant event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Asset-related grant</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Deferred income, amortised over the asset's useful life</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Income-related grant</span><span><span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Matched to related costs, or recognised immediately</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 4</span><span>Fixed Assets — supplies the useful life basis for amortising asset-related grants</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Deferred income (grants)</div><div class="glossary-def">A liability recognised for an asset-related government grant, amortised systematically to profit or loss over the related asset's useful life.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Grant related to income</div><div class="glossary-def">A government grant not tied to the formation of a long-term asset, recognised in profit or loss matched to the related costs or immediately if compensating for costs already incurred.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe16 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
